findings.text:
The supplier is financially strained:
- credit index worsened from 230 to 302;
- equity ratio 20%;
- it is negotiating with its banks;
- it has introduced short-time work;
- the MD said 'cannot sign anything that lowers margin'.
Room for a price cut is minimal, and squeezing it adds supply risk. Volume (8,670 vs 7,040 pcs) and cash are its real needs.
